              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "währenddessen — \"in the meantime, while that was going on\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sie telefonierte. Währenddessen kochte das Wasser. She was on the phone. In the meantime the water boiled."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Built on während. As an adverb, the verb comes second after it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "währenddessen joins während \"during\", the present participle of währen \"to last\" (EtymDB), and dessen \"of that\": while that lasted."
            }
          ]
        },
